{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>She is brought out.</b> To be burned." "<b>And she sent to her father-in-law.</b> She did not want to whitewash his face and say, 'I am pregnant by you,' but rather 'by the man to whom these belong' — she said: if he acknowledges, he acknowledges of himself; and if not, let them burn me, and I will not whitewash his face. From here the Sages said: better for a person to be cast into a fiery furnace than to whitewash his fellow's face in public." "<b>Recognize, please.</b> נָא is nothing but a term of request — 'recognize, please, your creator,' and do not destroy three lives."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:40.122408832Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}